---
source: crates/ym-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"info\"])"
---
Print metadata and the automatic estimates without rendering

Usage: ym info [OPTIONS] <FILES>...

Arguments:
  <FILES>...  ARW files to inspect

Options:
      --json
          Print one JSON object per file instead of text (the shape of `render --json` without `output` and `timings_ms`)
  -q, --quiet
          Print only errors on stderr
      --profile <ID>
          Force a camera profile, for comparisons (for example `sony-ilce-7rm4`)
  -v, --verbose
          Print what is happening on stderr: stages, timings and notes
      --auto-provider <yellowmoon|apple|claude|agy>
          Who grades each photo's Auto for this run: yellowmoon (Yellowmoon's own Auto), apple (Apple Intelligence), claude (Claude Code) or agy (Antigravity). Default: the app's setting. Naming claude or agy is your consent for this run: ym sends a 768 px picture of each photo and the instructions to that service, through the program installed on this computer. Answers from Claude Code and Antigravity can differ from run to run
      --apple-auto <on|off>
          The old name of --auto-provider: on is apple, off is yellowmoon. Not with --auto-provider
      --auto-instructions <FILE>
          A text file with instructions for the model, used for this run instead of those in Preferences (at most 2000 characters; an empty file is the default instructions). Also called --apple-auto-instructions
      --suggest-crop[=<ASPECT>]
          Also print Auto crop's proposal: the straighten angle and the frame for an aspect (original, free, 1:1, 4:5 or 16:9; original when none is given), for the photo as the camera turned it
  -h, --help
          Print help
